Tournament Attention Analysis
Connecting tournament theory to transformer attention patterns
Based on analysis of Napolitano (2026) paper


============================================================
KILLING FORM COMPARISON: so(n) vs gl(n,R)
============================================================

n = 3:
  so(3): dim = 3, Killing eigenvalue = -2, signature = (0, 3, 0)
  gl(3,R): dim = 9, Killing signature on sl = (5, 3, 1)
  'Active' (negative) = 3 = dim(so(3)) = 3: MATCH
  'Dark' (positive) = 5, null = 1
  Napolitano ratio: dark/active = 5/3 = 1.667

n = 5:
  so(5): dim = 10, Killing eigenvalue = -6, signature = (0, 10, 0)
  gl(5,R): dim = 25, Killing signature on sl = (14, 10, 1)
  'Active' (negative) = 10 = dim(so(5)) = 10: MATCH
  'Dark' (positive) = 14, null = 1
  Napolitano ratio: dark/active = 14/10 = 1.400

n = 7:
  so(7): dim = 21, Killing eigenvalue = -10, signature = (0, 21, 0)
  gl(7,R): dim = 49, Killing signature on sl = (27, 21, 1)
  'Active' (negative) = 21 = dim(so(7)) = 21: MATCH
  'Dark' (positive) = 27, null = 1
  Napolitano ratio: dark/active = 27/21 = 1.286

n = 11:
  so(11): dim = 55, Killing eigenvalue = -18, signature = (0, 55, 0)
  gl(11,R): dim = 121, Killing signature on sl = (65, 55, 1)
  'Active' (negative) = 55 = dim(so(11)) = 55: MATCH
  'Dark' (positive) = 65, null = 1
  Napolitano ratio: dark/active = 65/55 = 1.182


